  "implementation_change": "Keep supported native kernel pools at one thread throughout the owned run, restore caller limits after joining all tasks, and retain the configured outer assembly/study budget. Remove per-batch native-library scans and pool reconfiguration.",
  "findings": [
    "Four actual assembly workers were recorded for every four-CPU run; sparse factorization remained serial.",
    "Electrical/thermal assembly is a limited fraction of total time; serial sparse solves, reporting and memory-bound array work dominate.",
    "The two-repeat ranges overlap strongly. These observed medians do not establish a stable speedup ranking or attribute the complete historical slowdown to one cause."
  ],
  "mesh_verified": false,
  "limitations": "Two fresh-process repetitions per revision/budget in alternating order. Other task agents were reserved from heavy calculations; background system load, temperature and CPU frequency were not controlled. Process RSS excludes the preparation parent. Same-mesh equality is not mesh convergence; no universal speedup guarantee.",
